    <!-- Guide Screen -->
    <string name="guide_title">HyperOS Unlock Guide</string>

    <string name="guide_step1_title">1. How to get new_bbs_serviceToken</string>
    <string name="guide_step1_body">Install firefox browser on your phone\nInstall cookie-editor extension\nGo to c.mi.com/global\nOpen the cookie-editor extension and look for new_bbs_serviceToken\nCopy the value and paste it into the app</string>

    <string name="guide_step2_title">2. Prerequisites &amp; Rules</string>
    <string name="guide_step2_body">• Xiaomi Account must be active for at least 30 days.\n• HyperOS Global/EEA/ID/TW/RU are supported (Mainland China CNXM is excluded).\n• Xiaomi enforces a daily quota limit (~1500 devices) resetting at exactly 00:00:00 Beijing Time.\n• Once approved, unlock authorization remains valid for 1 year.</string>

    <string name="guide_step3_title">3. Binding Device in Developer Options</string>
    <string name="guide_step3_body">• After receiving approval in Xiaomi Unlock Tool, wait 1-2 minutes.\n• Turn OFF Wi-Fi and turn ON Mobile Data (SIM card with active data connection is required by Xiaomi).\n• Go to Settings > Additional Settings > Developer Options.\n• Tap \'Mi Unlock Status\' > tap \'Add account and device\'.\n• If successful, Xiaomi will show the standard waiting period (usually 72 hours / 168 hours).</string>

    <string name="guide_step4_title">4. Common Errors &amp; Solutions</string>
    <string name="guide_step4_body">• \"Couldn\'t add. Please go to Mi Community to apply\": Daily 1500 device quota reached. Try again next day at 00:00:00 Beijing time with Auto Mode.\n• \"System is being upgraded. Please try again later\": Common glitch on Redmi Note 13 series. Retry later.\n• \"Code 100004 / Token expired\": Your web session ended. Generate a fresh new_bbs_serviceToken.</string>

